  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="bf2a-1d31-9689-21a5" name="Early Horse Nomads (Art of War) - List Notes" publicationId="b792-78e1-7b03-d4d6" hidden="false">
      <description>EARLY HORSE NOMADS (The Art of War, p.32): the mounted nomads (hu / Quanrong) who raided China from the 5th century BCE. Percentage limits are by points. "May only have one selected option per 1,000 points" for Special Units is documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Early Horse Nomads]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Cavalry: at least 33%
  Infantry: up to 33%
  EARLY HORSE NOMADS. Characters up to 33% (the army should include at least one character to lead it). Cavalry at least 33%. Infantry up to 33%.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
